 runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids January to February came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 that middle sat at 42% of normal in both February to March and November to December. Every one of the 6 grids had its driest year in 1953, as low as 51%. On grid 20850 the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 is 61.1, and that one is not final yet.</p>"}
